            <ArticleTitle>Antioxidants: Wonder drugs or quackery?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>785-788</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/biof.1388</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An answer to the question posed by the title must be simple not to disturb in his tomb Albert Einstein, who wrote &quot;Man muß die Dinge so einfach wie möglich machen. Aber nicht einfacher&quot;. A simple answer (not simpler) can be: Antioxidants are not antioxidants, they are not wonder drugs and they are not all quackery; but they are not nothing. The arguments in support of this conundrumic statement will be developed below. © 2017 BioFactors, 43(6):785-788, 2017.</AbstractText>
